". But the tool \'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\' might have restrictions. Let me check the tool\'s description again. The tool says that interactive commands are not supported, like "kubectl edit", and interactive flags like "-it" are not allowed. However, the "kubectl logs" command doesn\'t use interactive flags. The previous error was because of using "-it" in the exec command, which is for interactive shells. But logs don\'t need that. \n\nWait, in the previous attempt, the user tried to run "kubectl exec -it ...", which is why the -it flag was rejected. Now, the command is "kubectl logs", which doesn\'t have interactive flags. So the correct command should be "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x -n hotel-reservation". The tool \'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\' can handle this as it\'s a non-interactive command. \n\nTherefore, the next tool call should be to exec_kubectl_cmd_safely with the logs command. This will retrieve the logs and help identify the root cause of the crash. If the logs show an error like "command not found" for \'rate\', that would confirm the earlier suspicion about the missing binary. Alternatively, other errors in the logs could point to different issues. Once the logs are retrieved, the user can analyze them to proceed with the mitigation.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-9beb64130808a337', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 498, 'prompt_tokens': 5087, 'total_tokens': 5585, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc91-e14a-7a92-9d32-33099baf2e7a-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'com