t the service\'s YAML. Let me try that. The command would be \'kubectl get service mongodb-rate -n hotel-reservation -o yaml\'. That should show the service\'s configuration, including endpoints and selectors. If the service doesn\'t exist, it will throw an error, but if it does, it will display the details. Let\'s try that.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\n\nJustification: The service "mongodb-rate" was not found, so I need to directly retrieve its YAML configuration to verify its existence, endpoints, and selectors. This will clarify whether the service is misconfigured or missing, which could prevent the \'rate\' service from connecting to MongoDB.\n\ntool_call: \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl get service mongodb-rate -n hotel-reservation -o yaml"\n  }\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 752, 'prompt_tokens': 9477, 'total_tokens': 10229, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc92-f481-7d22-bef8-0ef6211c9580-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 9477, 'output_tokens': 752, 'total_tokens': 10229}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='27e82a73-858b-497f-9cc9-6faffbe6688c'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to diagnose why the \'rate\' microservice is crashing. They\'ve already checked the logs and found that the service is trying to connect to MongoDB at mongodb-rate:27017. The MongoDB pod is running, but the service might not be properly configured.\n\nEarlier, they tried to get the endpoints for mongodb-rate, but that tool didn\'t exist. Then they tried describing the service, but it wasn\'t found. Now, they\'re trying to get the service\'s YAML configuration. If the service doesn\'t exist, that would explain why the \'rate\' service can\'t connect. \n\nWait, the user just tried to get the service\'s YAML with kubectl get service mongodb-rate -n hotel-reservation -o yaml, but the response was an error. The error message says "services "mongodb-rate" not found". That means the service doesn\'t exist in the namespace. But earlier, they saw a pod named mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz, which is part of the mongodb-rate deployment. \n\nSo, the problem might be that the MongoDB service isn\'t created. The pod is running, but without a service, other pods can\'t connect to it. The \'rate\' service is trying to connect to mongodb-rate:27017, which is the service name, but if the service isn\'t there, the connection fails. \n\nThe next step is to check if the MongoDB service exists. Since the user can\'t use get_endpoints, they need to use kubectl to describe or get the service. But since the service isn\'t found, they should check the deployments and services in the namespace to see if mongodb-rate is listed. Maybe the service was never created, or it\'s misconfigured. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the service exists but has no endpoints because the pod isn\'t selecting it. The user should check the service\'s YAML to see the selector and ports. If the service is missing, they need to create it. But since the user is using the exec_kubectl_cmd_safely tool, they can try to get the service\'s YAML again to confirm. \n\nWait, the previous attempt to get the service\'s YAML resulted in an error because the service doesn\'t exist. So the conclusion is that the MongoDB service is missing. That would explain why the \'rate\' service can\'t connect. The solution would be to create the MongoDB service with the correct selector and port. \n\nBut the user\'s tools don\'t include a way to create services, so they might need to inform the user that the service is missing and needs to be created. However, the current tools only allow querying, not modifying. So the final answer would be that the MongoDB service is missing, leading to the \'rate\' service\'s connection failure.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl get service mongodb-rate -n hotel-reservation -o yaml"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b1e7c09e7b30ac94', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 624, 'prompt_tokens': 10615, 'total_tokens': 11239, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc93-196d-7960-81e3-5be4b2805c33-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl get service mongodb-rate -n hotel-reservation -o yaml'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-b1e7c09e7b30ac94', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 10615, 'output_tokens': 624, 'total_tokens': 11239}), ToolMessage(content='Command Rejected: Error executing kubectl command:\nError from server (NotFound): services "mongodb-rate" not found\n', id='e38b58b1-85ab-4ae5-accc-e8bc3633d07a', tool_call_id='chatcmpl-tool-b1e7c09e7b30ac94'), HumanMessage(content='You are now in the thinking stage. Choose a tool from the available tools and justify your choice.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='e87c5d8b-b76d-4233-aa68-1432cdbb1206'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let\'s try to figure out why the \'rate\' microservice is crashing. The user has already checked the logs and found that the \'rate\' service is trying to connect to MongoDB at mongodb-rate:27017. The MongoDB pod is running, but the service might not be properly set up.\n\nFirst, the user tr