then checked the MongoDB pod's status and logs, which showed the MongoDB service was running but the 'rate' service wasn't connecting. The user tried to get the MongoDB service details but found that the service wasn't created. \n\nThey then created the MongoDB service 'mongodb-rate' manually, which was successful. After creating the service, they checked the endpoints and confirmed that the service was correctly pointing to the MongoDB pod. Now, they need to verify if the 'rate' service can connect to MongoDB by checking the logs again.\n\nThe latest step was to check the 'rate' pod's logs again. If the logs now show no errors and the pod is running, the issue is resolved. If there are still errors, it might be a problem with the 'rate' service's configuration or application code. Since the MongoDB service is now correctly set up, the next logical step is to confirm the 'rate' service's connectivity and application health.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-948a22c75aa76194', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 395, 'prompt_tokens': 12990, 'total_tokens': 13385, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc94-1bd7-7b01-bcd2-fdf3561642a0-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-948a22c75aa76194', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12990, 'output_tokens': 395, 'total_tokens': 13385}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T16:12:27Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"