tl_cmd_safely\' can list pods) would help. Wait, the available tools include \'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\', so I can use that to run \'kubectl get pods\' in the namespace to get the current pod names.\n\nOnce I have the correct pod name, I can then proceed to check the filesystem. Also, maybe the pod is in a CrashLoopBackOff state, so the name might include a different suffix like \'-1\' or \'-2\'. Alternatively, the pod might not be running, so the name might not be available yet. \n\nSo the next step is to retrieve the list of pods in the hotel-reservation namespace to find the correct name. Then, use that name in subsequent commands. Let me structure the tool call to get the pods.\n</think>\n\ntool name: exec_kubectl_cmd_safely\n\nJustification: The pod "hotel-reservation-rate-0" was not found, so I need to first verify the current pod names in the "hotel-reservation" namespace to identify the correct target. This will ensure the subsequent commands use an accurate pod name.\n\ntool_call: \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl get pods -n hotel-reservation"\n  }\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 417, 'prompt_tokens': 3003, 'total_tokens': 3420, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc91-a30b-78b3-8ebd-cce3a4066d41-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 3003, 'output_tokens': 417, 'total_tokens': 3420}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='aa08d423-0fa9-4455-bf5c-8b48e4f36a33'), AIMessage(content='<think>\nOkay, let me try to figure out what\'s going on here. The user is trying to debug the \'rate\' microservice in the hotel-res