d to run `kubectl logs` on the specific pod. However, the user\'s goal is to check if the pod is running. \n\nWait, the user\'s last tool call was to get the pod, but it was rejected. The error message says "Command Rejected (ValueError): Pipe commands are forbidden". But the command they used didn\'t have a pipe. Wait, looking back, the user\'s previous command was `kubectl get pod mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz -n hotel-reservation`, which doesn\'t have a pipe. So why was it rejected? Maybe the system is enforcing no pipes, but the command doesn\'t have any. \n\nHmm, maybe the user made a typo in the pod name. Let me check again. The pod name in the list is `mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz`. So the command is correct. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user needs to check the MongoDB pod\'s status using `kubectl describe` to see if there are any issues. But the user can\'t use pipes, so they have to run the command directly. \n\nWait, the user\'s last tool call was to get the pod, and the system rejected it. But the command doesn\'t have a pipe. Maybe the system is rejecting it for another reason. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the user should check the MongoDB pod\'s logs to see if it\'s running. So the next step would be to run `kubectl logs mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz -n hotel-reservation` to check for any errors in the MongoDB service. That would help determine if the MongoDB pod is healthy and why the \'rate\' service might be crashing. \n\nBut the user can\'t use pipes, so they need to run the command directly. The correct approach is to check the MongoDB pod\'s logs to see if there are any errors preventing it from running. If the MongoDB pod is not running, that would explain the \'rate\' service\'s crash. \n\nSo the next tool call should be to get the logs of the MongoDB pod. That would help identify if there\'s an issue with MongoDB itself. If MongoDB is down, the \'rate\' service can\'t connect, leading to a crash. \n\nTherefore, the user should use `exec_kubectl_cmd_safely` to run `kubectl logs mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz -n hotel-reservation` to check the MongoDB logs for any errors.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-acc0d5f0f8024e45', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 1050, 'prompt_tokens': 5924, 'total_tokens': 6974, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc92-3f87-75b1-895f-b278952ff447-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-acc0d5f0f8024e45', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 5924, 'output_tokens': 1050, 'total_tokens': 6974}), ToolMessage(content='{"t":{"$date":"2026-03-17T16:08:27.086+00:00"},"s":"I",  "c":"CONTROL",  "id":23285,   "ctx":"main","msg":"Automatically disabling TLS 1.0, to force-enable TLS 1.0 specify --sslDisabledProtocols \'none\'"}\n{"t":{"$date":"2026-03-17T16:08:27.090+00:00"},"s":"W",  "c":"ASIO",     "id":22601,   "ctx":"main","msg":"No TransportLayer configured during NetworkInterface startup"}\n{"t":{"$date":"2026-03-17T16:08:27.090+00:00"},"s":"I",  "c":"NETWORK",  "id":4648601, "ctx":"main","msg":"Implicit TCP FastOpen unavailable. If TCP FastOpen is required, set tcpFastOpenServer, tcpFastOpenClient, and tcpFastOpenQueueSize."}\n{"t":{"$date":"2026-03-17T16:08:27.091+00:00"},"s":"I",  "c":"STORAGE",  "id":4615611, "ctx":"initandlisten","msg":"MongoDB starting","attr":{"pid":1,"port":27017,"dbPath":"/data/db","architecture":"64-bit","host":"mongodb-rate-bfbcf4587-km8wz"}}\n{"t":{"$date"