\nJustification: The MongoDB service `mongodb-rate` is now correctly exposing the pod\'s endpoint (`10.244.0.218:27017`). To confirm the \'rate\' service can connect to MongoDB, I will check the \'rate\' pod\'s logs again. If no errors are present, the issue is resolved. If errors persist, further investigation into the \'rate\' service\'s configuration or application code is required.\n\ntool_call: \n{\n  "tool": "exec_kubectl_cmd_safely",\n  "args": {\n    "command": "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x -n hotel-reservation"\n  }\n}', additional_kwargs={'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 779, 'prompt_tokens': 11807, 'total_tokens': 12586, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'stop', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc93-f4c7-7d12-9b26-c32f9cf59e7c-0', tool_calls=[], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 11807, 'output_tokens': 779, 'total_tokens': 12586}), HumanMessage(content='Now generate a tool call according to your last chosen tool.', additional_kwargs={}, response_metadata={}, id='0ec77cca-f864-49ee-83c5-8f76f0dbc268'), AIMessage(content="<think>\nOkay, let me recap what's been done so far. The user is dealing with a fault in the 'rate' microservice of the hotel reservation application. The initial issue was that the 'rate' pod was in a CrashLoopBackOff state with exit code 2. \n\nFirst, they checked the pods and found that the 'rate' pod wasn't running. They tried to exec into the pod to check for the 'rate' binary but faced issues with interactive commands and pod names. Then, they retrieved the list of pods and found the correct pod name: 'rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x'. \n\nNext, they checked the logs of the 'rate' pod and saw some initial messages but no errors. They then checked the MongoDB pod's status and logs, which showed the MongoDB service was running but the 'rate' service wasn't connecting. The user tried to get the MongoDB service details but found that the service wasn't created. \n\nThey then created the MongoDB service 'mongodb-rate' manually, which was successful. After creating the service, they checked the endpoints and confirmed that the service was correctly pointing to the MongoDB pod. Now, they need to verify if the 'rate' service can connect to MongoDB by checking the logs again.\n\nThe latest step was to check the 'rate' pod's logs again. If the logs now show no errors and the pod is running, the issue is resolved. If there are still errors, it might be a problem with the 'rate' service's configuration or application code. Since the MongoDB service is now correctly set up, the next logical step is to confirm the 'rate' service's connectivity and application health.\n</think>\n\n", additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{"command": "kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x -n hotel-reservation"}', 'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-948a22c75aa76194', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 395, 'prompt_tokens': 12990, 'total_tokens': 13385, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfc94-1bd7-7b01-bcd2-fdf3561642a0-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'exec_kubectl_cmd_safely', 'args': {'command': 'kubectl logs rate-6fff88f6f5-zr48x -n hotel-reservation'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-948a22c75aa76194', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 12990, 'output_tokens': 395, 'total_tokens': 13385}), ToolMessage(content='{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T16:12:27Z","message":"TLS disabled."}\n{"level":"info","time":"2026-03-17T16:12:27Z","message":"Set global log level